    {
      "data": {
        "text": "**Choosing the Implementation**\n\nI've decided to move forward with AWS SQS using `boto3` for the Python implementation. This will allow for robust and scalable dead-letter queue management.\n\n\n**Defining the Python Script**\n\nI am now focused on defining the contents of the `dead_letter.py` file. I plan to use `write` to create it, embedding comments within the code to explain the use of `boto3` and the AWS SQS integration. The script will send messages to an SQS queue which will act as the dead-letter queue.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789860277943,
          "start": 1789860275364
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bbfc64a4001EDXiwYsdhMijhZ",
      "message_id": "msg_0bbfc612b001VnVQcSK4mYXomX",
      "session_id": "ses_f44039ee5ffe3N71D8apoyX1Jp",
